WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:03.194
Unit seven. Understanding Emotions!

2
00:00:04.177 --> 00:00:07.512
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Visal, your school doctor.

3
00:00:07.562 --> 00:00:10.825
Hi, Doctor Visal! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:10.875 --> 00:00:14.515
Today we learn about Understanding Emotions. Let's go!

5
00:00:15.455 --> 00:00:19.255
Emotions. Say it with me. Emotions!

6
00:00:22.687 --> 00:00:25.937
Triggers. Say it with me. Triggers!

7
00:00:29.478 --> 00:00:33.361
Body signals. Say it with me. Body signals!

8
00:00:36.852 --> 00:00:40.052
Name it. Say it with me. Name it!

9
00:00:43.591 --> 00:00:47.157
Regulation. Say it with me. Regulation!

10
00:00:50.642 --> 00:00:53.676
Journal. Say it with me. Journal!

11
00:00:57.125 --> 00:00:59.908
Calm. Say it with me. Calm!

12
00:01:03.451 --> 00:01:06.735
Support. Say it with me. Support!

13
00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:20.666
Emotions often start with triggers and show up as body signals. Being able to name it — 'I feel anxious' — helps emotional regulation. A journal and support can help me stay calm.

14
00:01:20.716 --> 00:01:23.613
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Visal!

15
00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:29.921
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:29.971 --> 00:01:31.136
Body signals!

17
00:01:32.169 --> 00:01:37.189
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:37.239 --> 00:01:38.333
Calm!

19
00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:43.651
Did you know? Simply naming an emotion can help reduce how strongly you feel it!

20
00:01:43.701 --> 00:01:45.733
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:47.216 --> 00:01:55.128
Think and answer. What body signals tell you that you are stressed?

22
00:01:55.178 --> 00:01:56.328
Great answer!

23
00:01:57.432 --> 00:02:02.162
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:02.212 --> 00:02:04.799
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

